{
  "name": "bedmaker",
  "display_name": "BedMaker (under-bed twin arms)",
  "task": "Two arms that ride rails under the bed frame pull the sheet and comforter straight, put the pillows back and smooth the bed, then fold away out of sight.",
  "trigger": {
    "type": "phone_button",
    "label": "Make the bed",
    "options": [
      "Fold top edge back: yes / no",
      "Pillows: sleeping only / sleeping + decorative"
    ],
    "notify_on": [
      "done",
      "blocked",
      "needs_help"
    ]
  },
  "form_factor": "arm_on_rail",
  "footprint_m": [
    2.1,
    2.08
  ],
  "height_m": 1.07,
  "reach_m": 1.1,
  "payload_kg": 2,
  "speed_mps": 0.25,
  "battery_h": 0,
  "bom_usd": 10800,
  "bom_assumptions": "Prototype, quantity-1, 2026 street prices. Arms: 6 quasi-direct-drive actuators each (2 x ~$700 shoulder/elbow, 4 x ~$300 wrist) + structure + driver board. Rails: 2 x 1.95 m belt-driven linear axes with motor and driver. Grippers: soft two-finger pinch gripper with resistive tactile pads. Rest: headboard depth camera (~$335), 2 wrist cameras, Jetson Orin NX 16GB compute (~$900), 4 bed-leg load cells, 48 V wall supply, e-stop, skirt. Wall-powered, so battery_h is 0.",
  "cost_drivers": [
    [
      "2 x 6-DOF arms, ~1.1 m reach, built from off-the-shelf actuators",
      6600
    ],
    [
      "2 x 1.95 m belt-driven linear rails with carriages and motors",
      1200
    ],
    [
      "2 x soft fabric grippers with tactile fingertips",
      1100
    ]
  ],
  "env_changes_required": [
    "Bed frame needs >=15 cm clearance under the side rails for the folded arms (the primary bed has 0.15 m, so it just fits; low-profile or storage-drawer frames need the kit's own frame).",
    "Move both nightstands >=10 cm away from the bed sides; today the gap is ~5 cm and the arms need it to rise beside the mattress at the head end (cheap: just move them).",
    "Use a fitted sheet with elastic all round plus corner straps, so it never comes off and the robot never has to re-seat corners (cheap: ~$20).",
    "Sew or clip contrasting tabs on the comforter's four corners so the cameras find corners reliably on any pattern (cheap: ~$10).",
    "Keep the bed bench >=20 cm off the foot of the bed so the comforter can hang evenly.",
    "Mount the depth camera on top of the headboard and run power from the wall outlet behind the bed."
  ],
  "tasks_excluded": [
    "Re-seating fitted-sheet corners: means lifting a mattress corner while stretching elastic; replaced by a strapped fitted sheet (env change).",
    "Tucking the flat sheet / hospital corners: forcing fabric between a loaded mattress and the frame is not reliably solved; the sheet is pulled up and left untucked.",
    "Fluffing pillows: little visible benefit and hard to do well; pillows are only picked up and put back in place.",
    "Stripping and changing sheets (stretch goal): handling a full set of loose fabric and putting on a fitted sheet is beyond reliable manipulation today.",
    "Scheduled or automatic start (after alarm, bed empty for X min): team rule is on-demand only, so it starts from the phone button.",
    "Moving non-bedding objects (phone, book, stuffed animal): the grippers are built for pinching fabric, not rigid objects, so it stops and asks the user to clear them.",
    "Picking a comforter up off the floor: out of reach of rails under the bed; it notifies the user."
  ],
